>    "you can harass someone and not get caught".  Okay, the instructions

	Again, information is typically legal, even if actions aren't.
You were correct to deal with the systems issue, (port 25), not the
distribution issue (banning such info would prevent people from
resending RISKS digest).

>1-A.)  Commercial advertising should be discouraged in .plans or .sigs.  
>       Racial or any other type of abuse should be prohibited.

	What's "abuse"? Even putting aside issues of censorship and
academic freedom, I think system administrators are buying too much
aggravation for themselves if they get into this sort of determination.
Everyone who loses a complaint will say "but you punished for that, look
how this is worse. You are really a against-my-group-ist". The winners
will just be encouraged to get more extreme, since they've won once, and
that sets local precedent. And the losers will never stop flaming.

